# Deriving ancestors in a small family
#
# Three parent links describe two family branches. Two forward N3 rules, one
# of them recursive, derive direct and indirect ancestors. The program has no
# log:query, so eyeron outputs every statement it derived: the four ancestor
# relationships.

@prefix : <https://eyereasoner.github.io/eyepl/examples/query#> .

# The family: alice -> bob -> carol, and dora -> emma
:alice :parentOf :bob .
:bob :parentOf :carol .
:dora :parentOf :emma .

# A parent is an ancestor
{
    ?x :parentOf ?y
} => {
    ?x :ancestorOf ?y
} .

# A parent of an ancestor is an ancestor too (the recursive rule)
{
    ?x :parentOf ?y .
    ?y :ancestorOf ?z
} => {
    ?x :ancestorOf ?z
} .
